4.  Core Feature Requirements

F-01  ·  Authentication & Onboarding

Requirements
Sign up via Email/Password or Google OAuth
Email verification before first session
Onboarding wizard (3 steps max): timezone, work categories, preferred session length
Public profile page at /profile/[username]

Constraints
Passwords hashed with bcrypt (rounds: 12)
JWT access token (15 min) + refresh token (7 days) in httpOnly cookie
No dark patterns on free tier — limits shown transparently

F-02  ·  Session Booking via Cal.com

Requirements
Each user gets a Cal.com booking page (auto-created on registration)
Booking page embedded in /schedule using @calcom/embed-react
Event types pre-configured: 25 min, 50 min, 75 min focus sessions
Cal.com webhook → our API on BOOKING_CREATED / BOOKING_CANCELLED / BOOKING_RESCHEDULED
Booking confirmation triggers email + dashboard session card
Users can share their Cal.com link directly with a partner

Integration Flow
User fills Cal.com form
  → Cal.com fires webhook → /api/webhooks/calcom
    → Parse booking payload
      → Create Session record in DB
        → Notify both participants (email + in-app)
          → 5 min before: reminder notification
            → Session room unlocked at start time


Business Rules
Free tier: max 3 bookings/week enforced at booking time via middleware
Partner can be: (a) a specific user by username, or (b) "any available" via queue
Cancellation requires ≥ 1 hour notice to avoid strike

F-03  ·  Matching Engine

Requirements
Users book a session by selecting a calendar slot
Time slots are available every 15 minutes
Multiple users can book the same slot
Users are matched in pairs of 2 within the same slot and duration
Matching is based on: same slot, same duration, no block relationship, active and not banned users
Categories and profile tags are collected for profile/session context only — not required for matching in MVP
If a slot has an odd number of bookings, the extra unmatched user remains pending
If no partner is found before the session start cutoff, the user is offered fallback options

Architecture
User books a slot
→ create booking request
→ find earliest unmatched booking in the same slot and duration
→ if found:
   create session for both users
   mark both bookings as matched
   notify both users
→ if not found:
   keep booking pending


F-04  ·  Live Session Room (LiveKit)

Requirements
Session room at /session/[sessionId] — entry only for booked participants
Session starts with a Goal Setting modal (15s timeout → auto-dismissed)
Video UI: partner tile (main), self tile (bottom-right), mute, camera, screen share
Timer counts down from session length — 5-min warning toast
Reflection modal on session end
Report / leave button always visible

