Token Generation (Backend)
// NestJS LiveKit Service
generateToken(sessionId: string, userId: string, userName: string): string {
  const token = new AccessToken(
    process.env.LIVEKIT_API_KEY,
    process.env.LIVEKIT_API_SECRET,
    { identity: userId, name: userName }
  );
  token.addGrant({
    roomJoin: true,
    room: sessionId,
    canPublish: true,
    canSubscribe: true,
    canPublishData: true,
  });
  return token.toJwt();
}


F-05  ·  Session Lifecycle Management

Session States
PENDING → CONFIRMED → ACTIVE → COMPLETED
                    ↘ CANCELLED
                    ↘ NO_SHOW


State Rules
ACTIVE: both users have joined the LiveKit room
NO_SHOW: one user never joined within 5 min of start time
COMPLETED: timer ends OR both users leave naturally
On COMPLETED: trigger Reflection modal, save, update stats
On NO_SHOW: after 3 incidents → account warning

