10.  Agent Instructions  (agent.md)
This section defines constraints for any AI coding agent working on this codebase.

Hard Constraints — Architecture
NEVER use REST where WebSocket is appropriate (session presence, match notifications)
NEVER store LiveKit tokens in localStorage — use in-memory state or server-side session
ALWAYS generate LiveKit tokens server-side (Express), NEVER on the client
ALWAYS verify Cal.com webhook signatures before processing
Session room name = session.id (UUID) — never use user IDs as room names

Hard Constraints — Code Style
All request payloads must be validated with a dedicated validation middleware or Zod schema
All Prisma queries must be wrapped in try/catch with proper error mapping
Use structured error responses (e.g. { error, statusCode }) consistently — never throw unhandled Errors
Frontend: no useEffect for data fetching — use React Query (TanStack Query)
All user-generated text must be sanitized before storage (DOMPurify or equivalent)

Hard Constraints — Database
NEVER run raw SQL — use Prisma query API only
All schema changes require a new migration file (never edit existing migrations)
Index on: sessions.status, sessions.scheduledAt, sessions.user1Id, sessions.user2Id

Hard Constraints — LiveKit
Always pass adaptiveStream: true and dynacast: true in RoomOptions
Screen share is always opt-in per session — NEVER auto-start
On room disconnect, attempt reconnect once before marking session as ended

Hard Constraints — Cal.com
Cal.com runs as a separate Docker service — NEVER couple its DB to ours
Communication is webhook-only (Cal.com → our API)
Store calcomBookingId on our Session model for idempotency checks

Hard Constraints — Business Logic
